    "change": {
      "implementation": "The resolution-local MethodLookupChainCache stores Vec<FqnId> rather than Vec<FullyQualifiedName>. A cache miss still delegates construction to the sole engine-owned method_lookup_chain, translates only owners that can exist in the ID-keyed graph/method stores, and exact method selection consumes the owner ID directly. A cache hit performs only the receiver namespace-existence lookup.",
      "semantic_boundary": "The cache remains private, resolution-local, and invalidated with the surrounding resolve pass. It does not expose IDs publicly, add a second MRO cache, merge engines, or move lookup policy out of engine resolution.",
      "test_instrumentation": "A cfg(test)-only NameRegistry counter proves that resolving a second method through an already cached Child-to-Parent chain performs exactly one fqn_id lookup rather than one lookup per cached owner. The counter is absent from production builds."
    },
